ub.io/BookOfProof/Translations/Translations.html)\nciteturn390search6 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 5 days ago; Please contact Richard Hammack if you have experience in translation and wish to translate Book of Proof into your language.\nTranslations\n\nCurrently there is only one translation of Book of Proof, into Turkish. Another into Brazilian Portuguese is nearing completion, and a Spanish translation is in the works.\nProposals for additional translations are welcome. But translation is a big project: More translations of Book of Proof have been begun and abandoned than completed. Serious inquiries only. Please contact Richard Hammack if you have experience in translation and wish to translate Book of Proof into your language. (As publisher, R. Hammack holds all translation rights; terms can be discussed.)\n\n  * Here is a link to the Turkish translation by Professors Mehmet Dagli and Oktay Olmez. If you have comments concerning this translation, please contact Professor Dagli at mdagli78@gmail.com. Any revisions will be posted here.--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nAdopters (https://richardhammack.github.io/BookOfProof/Adopters.html)\nciteturn390search7 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 5 days ago; It is difficult to track adoptions for an open textbook. ... Please contact me at rhammack@vcu.edu if you use Book of Proof in your courses, or if you have updates or corrections to the list. ... Richard Hammack ... University of California Santa Barbara  | USA  | Transition to Data Science, Probability and Statistics  | PSTAT 8  | 2022\nKnown Adoptions\n\nIt is difficult to track adoptions for an open textbook. I only know of one if an instructor or student emails me, or if I see a syllabus on line. Here is the list of adoptions, to the extent of my knowledge. I'd like for this list to be as complete as possible. Please contact me at rhammack@vcu.edu if you use Book of Proof in your courses, or if you have updates or correction